This held Root-only finalizer reuses the selected-file, exact-identity and
receipt mechanisms of the earlier ordinary-init finalizer. It is unexecuted.
It imports only Python standard-library modules, runs no commands, and changes
no existing evidence, canonical Source, plan, card, gates or Git state.

After Source review and actual comparison, Root may invoke:

    python -X utf8 -B finalize.py --approved-source-sha256 SOURCE_SHA --inputs PACKET_PATH#PACKET_SHA

The input packet schema is `ctf10-Init-postlude-finalization-inputs.v1`. Every
reference below is an actual path/SHA descriptor, with actual size when present:

- `native_completion`, `original_data_review`, `original_data_review_execution`;
- `formatted_inventory`, `source_correction`, `quality`, `candidate_workflow`;
- `comparison`, `comparison_execution`, `failed_native_workflow`,
  `failed_artifact_archive`;
- `source_preparations`: reviewed manifest refs under CTF-10 `*-prep-*` dirs;
- `recorded_outer_receipts`: rows `{role, execution, allowed_exit_codes}` for
  actual source-preserving Root launchers (distinct explicit exit expectations);
- `retained_lineage`: opaque actual Source/diff/application/correction/receipt
  refs; mutating outer receipts with Sourceguard=false belong only here;
- `prior_evidence`: prior committed small evidence/summary refs, including F/G
  or earlier history evidence if Root selects them. They are not replayed.

The four quality commands must actually return zero on the identical complete
raw current Source snapshot. Focused/workspace test counts come from genuine
stdout, with no predicted totals. The twelve canonical finals, original literal
archives, explicit non-formatter Clippy correction and refreshed own/API runtime
bindings must join that snapshot. Original and correction formatter receipts
remain distinct and may honestly have Sourceguard=false.

The released Native capture and fixed15/direct6 comparison retain their separate
Source identities. Candidate exits0/2 and comparator exits0/1 are preserved;
actual mismatch and required-unavailable records determine the reported selected
comparison status. A failing comparison remains failing evidence. No complete
whole-Init, persistent ordinary integration, CTF-10 or card-gate PASS is claimed.

Output is fresh `energyplus_porting_plan/evidence/CTF-10-init-postlude-comparison`
only: selected content-addressed objects, accepted.json, manifest.json and
summary.json. Existing `CTF-10-init-postlude` evidence stays untouched. Current
Native result/partition/log files and both candidate stdout files are full-byte
copies, without numerical JSON parsing or equation evaluation. Existing large
ordinary history traces and binaries/maps/weather/IDF payloads are excluded.
The archive explicitly does not claim a transitive replay closure; complete
Source-snapshot members are authenticated but only selected Source is stored.
All authenticated inputs are rechecked before and after storage. No results,
future hashes, receipts, counts or gate changes are supplied by this preparation.
